WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.330
Thank you for everything.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.180
Um...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.570
I've been prepared ever 
since Ginka awakened.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.810
In the end, this must 
have been her path.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.470
All of you, be careful.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.130
<b>The Moon's Light, The Sun's Shadow</b>

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.830
I don't know why

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.810
Ginka chose to disappear.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.610
I'm trying to understand it, but

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.850
this shouldn't have happened.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.500
Why? Why didn't she say anything?

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.170
Wasn't there anything we 
could have done for her?

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.530
This is what Ginka decided.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.280
There's no point in 
blaming yourself, Akari.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.440
But...

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.780
What would you have done 
if you were Ginka?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.660
I don't know. I'm not strong 
like you and Ginka.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.690
You are strong, Akari.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:39.420
Not everyone can face 
their feelings like that.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:45.520
Even if I'm scared, I let myself
 be driven by my hatred.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.380
What is it that I can do now?

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.830
As long as we don't understand 
the counterpart cards,

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.770
we'll have to research it ourselves.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:18.630
We don't know where 
Ginka-oneetan disappeared to,

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:22.110
so this is the best 
investigation we can do.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.490
I wonder if Ginka-oneetan 
went up into the sky.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.180
Being gloomy won't help anything.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.250
Let's do what we can.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.530
I wonder what's going to happen now?

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:44.430
What would you do if your 
counterpart card appeared?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.930
That's a hard question.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.290
Is there something we can do?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:59.280
Whatever you decide, is completely 
up to you, Priscilla.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:00.960
Yeah...

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.070
If there was something 
that I could do,

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:10.820
it would be to protect 
everyone as their senior.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.240
How's Luna?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.270
She hasn't come out yet.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.960
It's been three days now.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.610
<i>I could be next.</i>

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.640
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.310
Hello? Huh? Butler?

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.320
Well then...

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.800
Would it be all right to
 take Miss Luna back

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.420
into my care for the time being?

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:50.030
Yes. It's not the best solution,

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.330
but I believe it's better

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.990
than the current situation.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.890
I believe that if we 
go back to the villa

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:59.960
that she is familiar with, 
Milady will feel better.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.750
We shall keep in touch.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:04.760
Yes.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.010
Don't worry about anything else.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.120
Okay.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:13.890
So naive.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:19.650
Well, it'd be impossible for her 
to fight in that condition, meow.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.340
If she can build herself 
back up and come back,

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.730
she'll be a much more 
valuable asset, meow.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:24.920
Yeah.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.620
If Luna-san is able to recover,

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:33.200
the holes in everyone's 
hearts may start to heal.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:38.210
Hopefully it won't come to 
her not coming back at all.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.730
Have a safe trip, Luna-chan. 
Take care of yourself.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:45.950
Um...

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.950
Do you want to come with me, Akari-san?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.380
I'm sorry. It'd be great 
if I could go with you,

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.310
but right now, I want to 
think about what I can do here.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:05.570
If you were to disappear 
while I was gone...

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.070
It'll be okay.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:11.180
I won't disappear while you're gone.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.330
So get some rest and come 
back as your usual self soon.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:19.190
Akari-san...

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.070
It's been a while since I've 
been able to see you, Milady.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.770
Please get plenty of rest at the villa.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.120
Yes.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.400
I will keep this a secret 
from the main house.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.270
You don't need to worry 
about a thing, Milady.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.920
Thank you.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.450
<i>I wonder if Akari-san is scared.</i>

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.270
<i>Will she be okay even 
though I'm not there?</i>

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.500
I wonder if Luna-chan is okay.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.500
She needs to gather her thoughts.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.060
As soon as she calms down, 
things should go back to normal.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.150
<i>Hey, do you know the 
flower meaning for amaryllis?</i>

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.780
<i>Flower meaning?</i>

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.390
<i>It means "talkative."</i>

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.280
<i>I wish I could stay here and 
talk to you forever, Luna.</i>

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:38.280
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.550
Thank you.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.930
Have there been any leads 
regarding my sister?

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:59.570
Well, we have been searching 
everywhere, but...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.360
I see.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.930
I am terribly sorry.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.440
It's all right. I'm sorry.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.070
<i>Serena-oneechan!</i>

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.580
<i>Onee-chan...</i>

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.500
<i>So she disappeared?</i>

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.730
<i>Maybe it was a kidnapping 
for ransom money.</i>

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.450
<i>But there hasn't been any contact 
from a kidnapper, right?</i>

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:35.660
<i>She could be lying 
cold somewhere by now.</i>

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.770
<i>Well, that works out better for us.</i>

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.090
<i>You have a point.</i>

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:42.190
<i>This means a more distant relative 
could possibly become the heir.</i>

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.390
<i>How convenient.</i>

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.490
Don't you think you're 
fooling around too much?

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.300
You think so?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:10.170
I thought you were all 
enjoying this as well.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.730
There's nothing more painful 
than watching an obtrusive play.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.310
If you look at the big picture,

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:23.130
I don't think my goals
differ much from your own.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.150
Everyone's a critic...

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.240
<i>Awaken?</i>

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:41.870
<i>This is...</i>

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.930
<i>If you are able to see 
something that I cannot,</i>

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:58.590
<i>it means that the time has come.</i>

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.930
<i>I'm going to have to fight now?</i>

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.950
<i>What're you doing? Back us up!</i>

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.570
<i>I-I'm sorry!</i>

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.770
<i>Move!</i>

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.070
<i>I...</i>

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:31.500
<i>I can't do something this terrifying.</i>

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:34.900
<i>Serena-oneechan, save me!</i>

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:37.500
<i>Luna-chan!</i>

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.640
<i>It's because Akari-san 
was there for me.</i>

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.340
<i>But then...</i>

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:54.200
<i>Why am I...</i>

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:57.620
<i>Is it because she's so 
much like my sister?</i>

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:02.990
Onee-chan!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:11.810
Onee-chan!

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.540
Onee-chan...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:21.720
Luna-chan?

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.720
Akari-san?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.190
Sorry to show up so suddenly.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.980
I asked Etia-san to 
give me some time off.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:44.020
B-But what about Seira-san?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.870
Is she on her own?

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:50.190
She said she'd be fine with 
Meltina-san and Priscilla-san.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:51.500
I see...

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:56.420
I didn't think you'd actually come.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.920
Is it a bother?

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:03.670
A bother? I'm really 
happy! Thank you.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:09.220
But, since you've come for me,

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:13.140
does that mean we 
have to go back soon?

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.250
I don't want to go back.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.730
I want to stay here a little longer.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.730
There's no need to hurry.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:29.450
Akari-san...

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.190
We'll be waiting for you

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.270
until you're actually able to 
gather your thoughts.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.710
Until then,

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:37.900
I'll stay here with you.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:39.840
Really?

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:45.690
But then Seira-san...

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.590
Don't worry.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:56.020
Thank you for coming all 
the way from Nagataki.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.980
Oh, not at all.

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:03.830
I'm sure if you're here with her, 
Milady will feel much better.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:07.390
There are many places to 
play within this villa.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.990
Please enjoy.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:56.540
That's a pretty flower. 
What's it called?

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:01.540
Amaryllis. Its flower 
meaning is "talkative."

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.950
S-Sorry. Did I wake you?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.620
What's wrong? You can't sleep?

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.370
Yeah...

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.680
I see.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:45.340
Thank you for coming, really.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.290
Can I ask you something?

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:53.550
When you and Seira-san were 
talking that one time...

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.770
What were you talking about?

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:04.350
For Seira-san to cry like that...

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.530
What did you tell her, Akari-san?

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:16.240
I want to know more 
about you, Akari-san.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.340
I...

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.980
...want to know more about 
you too, Luna-chan.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:28.100
I still haven't been able to

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.190
sort out everything 
that happened that day,

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.110
so I don't know how 
to really talk about it.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.390
I'm really sorry.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.520
When I can actually talk 
about it, I'll tell you.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.030
O-Okay.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.930
Good night, then.

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.540
<i>Akari-san...</i>

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:12.170
<i>If possible, I'd like to stay 
with Akari-san like this forever.</i>

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:20.260
<i>I don't want her to disappear. 
I need to protect her.</i>

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.480
What? You want to go back?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:29.340
Yeah. I don't think it's right for me

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.820
to keep looking back.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.570
There's not much that I can do,

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.770
but I want to protect you, Akari-san.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:38.820
Luna-chan...

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.580
All right, let's go back together.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.590
Okay.

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:54.410
Please take this with 
you. It's a dummy card.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:56.090
A dummy card?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.820
It's a card with Elemental powers.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:02.840
If you use this against the counterpart 
card while you're fighting,

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:06.350
it'll think the dummy is you, 
so that'll be your chance...

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.780
So in the worst case scenario, 
you're telling us to run.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.700
It's very possible that 
the Daemonia that possess free will

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.610
will try to make 
the next move against us.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.070
Let's end this before Luna gets back.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.080
Let's go!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:28.500
Right!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.140
The moon is so pretty.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.670
Thank you.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.700
Thank you so much for coming.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.050
I'm so happy.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:48.510
As long as you're here, 
I don't need anything else.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:50.870
Luna-chan...

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:54.280
So I want to be with you forever.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.530
Even if I were to disappear,

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:02.600
you are someone very dear to me.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.240
A-Akari-san!

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:12.440
I'm flattered, but I'm sorry.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:16.010
I can't return your feelings, Luna-chan.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:21.370
Because I like Seira more 
than you, Luna-chan.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.250
If I'm going to fight 
alongside someone,

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:31.060
she'd be better than you, Luna-chan.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.290
Th-That's not what I meant.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.070
It's not? Then, what did you mean?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.910
You want Akari all to 
yourself, don't you?

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:45.160
But...

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:49.440
Do you know the other flower 
meaning that the amaryllis has?

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.830
Very strong vanity.

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:55.990
You act like you're not confident,

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:59.920
but you're vain in 
some ways, aren't you?

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:04.590
You want the ones who didn't accept you

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:07.140
to acknowledge your existence.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.140
You don't want to be treated 
like the tainted child.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.980
You don't want to lose to Seira.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.690
You want Akari to think highly of you.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.940
You want people to think highly 
of you. You want to be loved.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.200
Let all those feelings out.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.210
I...

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.040
<i>Luna is a tainted child anyway.</i>

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:43.570
I...

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:50.030
A-Akari-san...

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:58.830
Reversed, The Emperor means cruelty.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:03.900
I think it's very fitting 
for you right now.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.120
Huh.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.130
So this is what happens 
when you put a Daemonia

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:33.180
into an Elemental Tarot user.

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.970
I'm going to have 
you work really hard.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:47.230
Milady, Akari-sama, 
did you enjoy the lunar eclipse?

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:51.830
Milady?

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.580
This is strange.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:58.830
What is?

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.720
We were investigating Daemonia,

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:03.090
but we're also getting a response

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.670
from an Elemental Tarot at the same time.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.670
Time!

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.300
What does that mean?

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:11.310
It might be one of our comrades.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>The Emperor is a leader who leads 
by always looking ahead and is a 
symbol of authority within a society.</b>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:41.560
<b>#04 The Emperor</b>

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.060
We've known each other for so long,

00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:31.210
but we don't even know 
each other's hobbies.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.100
<b>Therefore, The Emperor card symbolizes 
an indomitable mental and physical ability 
that won't give in to any kind of situation.</b>

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:33.870
Can we really run Sefiro 
Fiore in this state?

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:35.890
Isn't there something more 
important than that?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:37.220
<b>If you were to choose this card, 
taking progressive actions with 
positive feelings and confidence 
will lead to success or the best 
results to eventually lead to success.</b>

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.020
It's vital to believe in each other, isn't it?

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:41.760
<b>However, if the card is reversed, 
it shows that because of your backward 
and negative attitude, you will miss your 
chance at attaining results as well as be 
met with animosity and distrust from 
others because of your pride.</b>

00:23:37.910 --> 00:23:41.370
<b>Like Burning Away</b>

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.560
That's right, Etia! Let us believe!

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.200
See you next time!
